55,156,157],"th",{},"Edition",[155,159,160],{},"How it updates",[162,163,164,173,186,193],"tbody",{},[152,165,166,170],{},[167,168,169],"td",{},"Desktop app (Windows, macOS, Linux x86_64 \u002F ARM64 \u002F ARMv7)",[167,171,172],{},"Checks every 10 minutes, downloads and installs the update in the background, then tells you; the new version starts with the next restart (tray → Restart, or quit and start).",[152,174,175,183],{},[167,176,177,178,182],{},"Headless (",[179,180,181],"code",{},"--serve",")",[167,184,185],{},"The same updater; on Windows the installer runs in passive mode. Restart the service to switch.",[152,187,188,190],{},[167,189,83],{},[167,191,192],{},"The phone checks the release at start and regularly, and installs the new APK (Android asks to confirm unless the app is device owner).",[152,194,195,198],{},[167,196,197],{},"Android (desktop UI)",[167,199,200],{},"Checks the release at start and every 10 minutes, downloads and verifies the new APK, then opens the Android installer to confirm. The first time Android asks to allow installing apps from Gateway Soft.",[134,202,203],{},"Every update is signed; the app refuses a file that was not signed with the Gateway Soft key.",[205,206,208],"h2",{"id":207},"update-by-hand","Update by hand",[134,210,211,212,215,216,219],{},"Download the installer of the new version and run it over the old one: settings, the session and the\nadded ports stay. On Linux install the new ",[179,213,214],{},".deb"," \u002F ",[179,217,218],{},".rpm"," the same way as the first time.",{"title":221,"searchDepth":222,"depth":222,"links":223},"",2,[224],{"id":207,"depth":222,"text":208},"How each edition updates itself and how to update by hand.","md",null,{},{"icon":49},{"title":46,"description":225},"BhfSQtRVGGfT2wIYjRoCRdu3filxT3S37gbMhIQ-ugw",[233,235],{"title":41,"path":42,"description":234},"Income, withdrawals and the sales statistics of your account.",{"title":51,"path":52,"description":236},"The usual problems and where to look first.",1794978314520]